{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "29", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "37", "S": "18"}}, "news": [{"title": "OCs issued but possession delayed as lifts & amenities not ready, say Jaypee Wish Town homebuyers", "para": "Residents of Wish Town are voicing serious concerns over the quality of construction and delays linked to Suraksha Group. They are pushing for a thorough investigation into whether the approved resolution plan for the stalled projects is being followed. Numerous buyers have pointed out the lack of essential services and infrastructure, making it difficult to occupy their flats.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/ocs-issued-but-possession-delayed-as-lifts-amenities-not-ready-say-jaypee-wish-town-homebuyers/134555687?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-259366/134555687.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "HSVP orders probe after two residential plots sold cheaper than regular ones in Gurugram", "para": "Haryana Shehri Vikas Pradhikaran is investigating the auction results of two residential corner plots in Gurgaon. The two corner plots sold for approximately half the price of general-category plots auctioned weeks earlier. An inquiry was initiated after discrepancies prompted concerns about the e-auction portal's integrity. Additionally, there was a delay in the issuance of the letter of intent for one of the plots.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/hsvp-orders-probe-after-two-residential-plots-sold-cheaper-than-regular-ones-in-gurugram/134555628?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-64638/134555628.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Washington State Investment Board backed fund exits \u20b9550 crore investment in Noida\u2019s Dasnac group", "para": "Kautilya Finance has successfully exited its investment in New Delhi-based Dasnac, realizing cash proceeds of Rs 550 crore. The investment relationship initiated in 2017 involved multiple financial years through various investment routes. Dasnac had raised Rs 420 crore from Kautilya Finance, which has now been fully repaid. The capital supported Dasnac\u2019s residential development projects in Noida, including significant developments.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/washington-state-investment-board-backed-fund-exits-550-crore-investment-in-noidas-dasnac-group/134555605?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103748/134555605.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}